// Atomic coordinates of one nucleotide of B-DNA, the fiber model of
// Chandrasekaran & Arnott (Landolt-Börnstein VII/1b, Table 2.4.4.2), as
// distributed with 3DNA v2.4 (x3dna-dssr/x3dna-v2.4, fiber/data/s04_bdna,
// commit 398cfcee57a7dfc7e1e7c3baec9a3643f821bbe3; BSD-3-Clause, see
// THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). Converted from nm to Å, hydrogens left out,
// atoms renamed to the NDB convention (O1/O2 → OP1/OP2, primes on sugar and
// backbone atoms, thymine ME → C7). Generated by a script; do not edit by hand.
//
// Model rules from the source table:
// - The nucleotide of the antiparallel strand is given by (r, −φ, −z), a
//   180° rotation about the x axis.
// - Successive nucleotides: add 36.0° to φ and 3.375 Å to z.
// - The listed O3' belongs to the neighbouring nucleotide on the P side; it
//   joins P (1.6 Å). The O3' bonded to this nucleotide's C3' is that atom
//   moved one step back (−36°, −3.375 Å) (3DNA README, "re-assign O3'").

